Fixed. The `break` on line 14 exited the loop after the first tracking param was deleted, so any subsequent tracking params (`fbclid` when `utm_source` came first, etc.) survived. Removing it lets the loop strip every present tracking param.

Verified behavior: a URL like `https://example.com/?utm_source=x&fbclid=y` now returns `https://example.com/` (both stripped) instead of leaving one behind.


